Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:03.00,注释,,0,0,0,,Part 1
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.78,0:00:12.78,场面文本,文本,0,0,0,,{\an9\fs30\fnTimes New Roman\b1\shad0\c&H151C23&\3c&H656B71&}Will my past self believe what I, his future self,\Ntells him? If only my mind goes back,\Nhow should I face Sylphie and Roxy? I want\Nto see them again, to spend more time with them.\NI want to tell them I'm sorry. But I can't\Nbear the thought of who I am now\Ntaking over the me from those happy days.\NShould I perform more experiments?\NSomething tells me I shouldn't.\NI don't know what a time paradox might do.\NSuppose I did go a few days into the past.\NIt's possible only my consciousness will go back,\Nleaving my memories behind in this world.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.78,0:00:12.78,场面文本,文本,0,0,0,,{\an7\fs30\fnTimes New Roman\b1\shad0\c&H151C23&\3c&H656B71&}I would be trapped living\Nin a pointless loop forever,\Nnot even able to die. If I'm going to risk it,\NI'd rather at least see Sylphie\Nand Roxy again, even justâ€”\NNo, forget it. No more agonizing over unknowns.\NI've got nothing left anyway.\NI failed to accomplish anything.\NI was a waste of skin.\NSo what if I fail and that has consequences?\NWhat do I care? Let it happen.\NBut if I pull it off, I might be able to\Nget one over on the Man-God.
